.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Enabling the debugger activates the server\(cqs
\f[CR]pre_command_hook\f[R] for breakpoint checking, which is separate
from the observe hook.
Both can be active simultaneously.
.IP \(bu 2
The debugger state is per\-session.
Enabling the debugger in one session does not affect other sessions.
.IP \(bu 2
If breakpoints were added in a previous enable/disable cycle, they are
cleared by \f[CR]bc_debug_disable()\f[R].
Re\-enabling starts with an empty breakpoint list.
.IP \(bu 2
The function blocks until the server acknowledges.
Use \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] for event processing, not for the enable
handshake.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: the client library is not thread\-safe.
Do not call \f[CR]bc_debug_enable()\f[R] concurrently with other
operations on the same \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R].
